<title>CANADA: Canada new housing price index falls in Sept.</title>
<headline>Canada new housing price index falls in Sept.</headline>
<dateline>OTTAWA 1996-11-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>Canada's new housing price index fell 2.0 percent in September to 131.5 (base 1986) from September 1995, Statistics Canada said on Friday.</p>
<p>    Index			 Sept     yr pct  month pct</p>
<p> Total			    131.5     -2.0	 unch</p>
<p> House only		     121.1     -2.3	 unch</p>
<p> Land only			165.2     -1.3	 -0.1</p>
<p>The index measures changes of contractors' selling prices of new residential houses.</p>
<p>A Reuter survey of economists had forecast a 0.1 percent rise in the annual index.</p>
<p>-- Reuters Ottawa Bureau 613-235-6745</p>
</text>
